Measured while answering #204's open questions, on the libgit2 1.9.3 that
Alien::Libgit2 carries here, with no git CLI in the picture (raw
Git::Native, git_remote_lookup + git_remote_push).

libgit2 honours the push URL -- both url.<base>.pushInsteadOf and an
explicit remote.<name>.pushurl -- on a real transport, and drops it on a
local path.

Over git:// (a `git daemon --enable=receive-pack` in front of two bare
repos A and B):

    url.git://127.0.0.1:9419/A/.insteadOf     = karrsplit:
    url.git://127.0.0.1:9419/B/.pushInsteadOf = karrsplit:
    remote probe = karrsplit:board.git

    fetch -> A       push -> B        # correct

    remote.probe.pushurl = git://127.0.0.1:9419/B/board.git
    fetch -> A       push -> B        # correct

The same two shapes with both sides as local bare-repo paths:

    fetch -> A       push -> A        # push URL dropped, push reports OK

It is not that the rewrite fails to happen. The push connects to the push
URL and only writes to the wrong one: with pushInsteadOf aimed at
ssh://pushtarget.invalid/ and insteadOf at a valid local path, the push
fails with "failed to resolve address for pushtarget.invalid" -- so the
push URL reached the transport. Aim it at a local path that does not exist
and the failure is "failed to resolve path .../nope/board.git", again the
push URL. Aim it at a local path that does exist and the connect succeeds,
after which the objects and refs land at the fetch URL instead. That
matches libgit2 local_push() opening remote->url rather than the
transport's own url.

Why it matters here: App::karr::Git->push is _push_refspecs -> $repo->remote
-> ->push, exactly the path measured, so a clone whose origin is a local
path and whose push URL differs publishes refs/karr/* to the fetch URL and
reports success. Silent, and the CLI fallback never runs because nothing
failed. Rare shape -- most boards sync over ssh or https, where libgit2 is
correct -- hence low.

Confirmed the config itself is right by pushing the same repo with git
2.47.3, which lands at the push URL in every one of these cases.

Not fixed under #204, which was scoped to the DESCRIPTION paragraph.
Options if this is worth acting on: detect a local-path remote carrying a
distinct push URL and route that push through the CLI fallback, or refuse
it with a named error rather than reporting a success that went elsewhere.
Fixed. Reproduced both shapes first (remote.<name>.pushurl and url.<base>.pushInsteadOf) by reading back which of two bare repos actually received refs/karr/*: push returned 1, the refs were in the fetch repo, the push repo empty.

_push_refspecs now checks the resolved push URL before handing the push to libgit2. libgit2 resolves it at git_remote_lookup time (pushurl with insteadOf applied, or pushInsteadOf against the fetch URL, NULL when neither is set), but Git::Native exposes only ->url and Git::Libgit2::FFI binds no git_remote_pushurl -- so App::karr::Git::_remote_pushurl reaches it through their shared FFI instance as a function object, never attached into their namespace.

Detection is three conditions: a push URL exists at all (NULL for every ordinary board -- one check, no string work), it differs from the fetch URL, and it is a local-transport path (_is_local_url: file:// yes, any other scheme no, a colon before the first slash is scp-style ssh, the rest is a path). Anything left over goes through the CLI fallback, which lands at the push URL. Under KARR_NO_CLI_FALLBACK there is no route, so it fails with a message naming both URLs -- the ticket's second option, kept for the case where the first is unavailable, rather than instead of it.

Chose routing over refusing: karr already keeps the CLI transport for ssh-config cases, so a correct route exists and refusing would be a refusal without need. ssh/https boards are untouched -- they have no push URL at all, so the check never gets past its first line.

Regression test t/208-push-local-push-url.t (7 subtests). Red probe with the fix reverted: subtests 1-3 fail (board lands in the fetch repo, no refusal, empty last_error) and the file dies at subtest 6. prove -l t/ : 184 files, 1290 tests, 0 skips, exit 0 (baseline 183/1283 plus this file's 7).

Also touched: the DESCRIPTION corner paragraph now says what karr does about it, =method push notes the route, Changes entry under {{$NEXT}}. Not committed.
